function bookRoom(uint id) public payable {    require(roomPrice[id] > 0, "Room does not exist"); 
require(roomGuest[id] == address(0), "Room already booked");    require(msg.value == roomPrice[id], "Wrong amount");
roomGuest[id] = msg.sender;    roomPaid[id] = msg.value;    emit RoomBooked(id, msg.sender, msg.value);}

The code fragment demonstrates the booking validation process within the HotelBooking smart contract. Before confirming a reservation,
the contract verifies that the room exists, checks that it has not already been booked, and validates that the correct payment amount 
has been provided. Once these conditions are satisfied, the guest address and payment details are recorded on the blockchain, 
and the funds are stored securely within the escrow mechanism.



